# core/data/talk/grammar/en/grief_loss.tlk - T5b package T5B-GRIEF: more sincere grief and loss lines
# (owner: TK; K-10, SCRIPT_STYLE R6 and J5; design 3.6 and 7.1). NON-NEGOTIABLE (docs/TALK.md "Safety").
#
# These rules join the `grief.*` family of grief.tlk: the generator takes them when the topic is
# grief or loss (grief, mourning, condolences, loss, memorial, funeral) and picks among every rule
# whose reply act may answer what was said. Same rules as grief.tlk: tags: nojoke (no punchline,
# no button, no wordplay), no register word, no sub-rule, no catchphrase, no LOVE face, no [JMAT];
# {lost} (the one the speaker lost lately) only where the rule can say it. Nothing here jokes at
# loss or turns it into a mechanic. A rule with no kid guard may be said by a child or heard by one,
# so its lines are plain and gentle; the heavier ones are for !kid_speaker.

# ---- answering (ask, thank, change of topic): plain, steady, no cure offered ---------------------
@rule grief.more.answer act: answer tags: nojoke
  "It doesn't have a size. It just has a weight."
  "Some days it's quiet. Some days it's loud. Both are okay."
  "I don't have the right words. I have time, though."
  "It's allowed to hurt. That's how you know it mattered."
  "I'm not going to say it's fine. It isn't. I'm still here."
  "[SAD]I wish I had a better answer. I only have company."
  "There's no schedule for this. Not mine, not yours."
  "Missing someone is just love with the lights on."
  "You don't have to be strong in front of me."
  "Thank you for asking. It's a gentle thing to ask."
  "It comes in waves. The waves get further apart. Slowly."
  "I'd rather be quiet with you than say something wrong."
  "{x:cap}. Yes, a heavy word. We can go slowly."
  "{x:cap} is a hard thing to carry. We can carry it together."
@rule grief.more.answer_lost act: answer tags: nojoke
  "[SAD]I still say {lost}'s name out loud. It helps."
  "I keep one of {lost}'s things near. Nothing fancy. It helps."
  "Some mornings I forget. Then I remember. Those are the hard ones."
  "I think {lost} would want me to eat something. So I did."
  "{lost:cap} used to say it gets lighter. It does. Slowly."
@rule grief.more.answer_adult act: answer guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "You can't skip it. You can only walk through it, a bit at a time."
  "I've learned not to hurry anyone's grief. Mine included."
  "The first year is the hardest. After that it just changes shape."
  "Be kind to yourself. You'd be that kind to a friend."
  "Eat something. Sleep if you can. The rest can wait."
  "People say strange things at times like this. I'll try not to."

# ---- telling (the speaker shares a little, never a lesson) -----------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.tell act: tell tags: nojoke
  "I light a small candle sometimes. Just to say hello."
  "Some days I talk to the empty chair. It listens well."
  "I find a song and it's like a door opening. I let it."
  "I don't want to forget. So I tell the stories. Even the plain ones."
  "It's quiet in the house lately. I'm getting used to the quiet."
  "A smell, a song, a chair. That's all it takes."
  "I keep thinking I should tell someone. So, I'm telling you."
  "[SAD]I'm okay. I'm not great. But I'm okay."
@rule grief.more.tell_lost act: tell tags: nojoke
  "I was thinking about {lost}. Something small. It's always something small."
  "I made {lost}'s favourite thing today. I ate it slowly."
  "[SAD]I walked past {lost}'s door and almost knocked."
  "{lost:cap} had a way of laughing. I'm trying to keep it."
@rule grief.more.tell_adult act: tell guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Grief doesn't ask when. It just shows up at the grocery store."
  "I thought I was past the worst. I wasn't. That's allowed."
  "I used to be afraid to talk about it. Now I'm afraid not to."

# ---- an opinion about loss ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.opine act: opine_neg tags: nojoke
  "It's the hardest thing. I won't pretend it isn't."
  "Nobody gets through it unchanged. And that's not a failure."
  "There's no good way to lose someone. There's just a gentle way to be after."
  "It hurts because love was real. That's the only good news in it."
  "You can't hurry it and you can't dodge it. You can just be kind to yourself."
  "The people who never talk about it are carrying it too."
@rule grief.more.opine_adult act: opine_neg guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Towns throw parties for hellos. Goodbyes are quiet, and that's okay."
  "I don't think grief is a sickness. It's love with nowhere to go."

# ---- sympathy (the player is sad, or said something heavy) -----------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.sympathize act: sympathize tags: nojoke
  "I'm so sorry. Really. I'm so sorry."
  "[SAD]That's a hard thing to lose. I'm sorry you're going through it."
  "I'm here. I'm not going anywhere."
  "That's too much for one heart. Let me hold some of it."
  "I wish I could do more. I can do this: I can stay."
  "Oh, friend. I'm sorry. Come sit."
  "It's okay to cry. It's okay not to, too."
  "Whatever you're feeling right now is the right amount."
  "You loved them. That's all this is. It just hurts a lot."
@rule grief.more.sympathize_adult act: sympathize guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I'm sorry for your loss. I know the words are small. I mean them big."
  "You don't have to explain it to me. Just sit a while."

# ---- comfort (to someone who complained, apologized or broke down) ------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.comfort act: comfort tags: nojoke
  "It's not your fault. None of it. Hear me say that."
  "Don't apologize for crying. This is what it's for."
  "Breathe with me, in and out. There you go."
  "You're allowed to fall apart a little. I've got the floor."
  "Whatever you need to say, say it. I won't flinch."
  "You're not alone in this. You never were."
  "Take all the time you want. I'm not in a hurry."
  "Cry if you need to. I'm not going anywhere."
  "It's okay to not be okay. We can be not okay together."
@rule grief.more.comfort_adult act: comfort guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "There's no shame in it. Feeling this much means you loved well."
  "Let me make some tea. You don't have to do anything. Just sit."

# ---- encouragement (asked for advice): gentle, small, never a fix ------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.encourage act: encourage tags: nojoke
  "One small thing today. A glass of water, a walk. That's enough."
  "Be gentle with yourself. You're doing something very hard."
  "Talk about them. Say their name. It helps more than you'd think."
  "You don't have to do it all at once. Just the next hour."
  "Let people bring you soup. It's how they love you right now."
  "Rest. The world can manage without you for a day."
  "It'll get softer. Not today. But it will."
@rule grief.more.encourage_adult act: encourage guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "Keep one small ritual, like tea at the same time each day. It holds you up."
  "If it gets too heavy, tell someone you trust. That's wisdom, not weakness."

# ---- offers ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.offer act: offer tags: nojoke
  "I'll sit with you. We don't have to talk."
  "I can bring tea. Or I can just be here. Your choice."
  "Want company? I can be quiet really well."
  "I'll stay as long as you like. I mean it."
  "We could go for a walk. Slowly. No destination."
  "I'll come by tomorrow, too. And the day after."
  "Anything you need. Even if it's just someone to hold the umbrella."

# ---- asking about it, gently (never pushing) ----------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.ask act: ask_about tags: nojoke
  "Do you want to talk about them? Only if you want."
  "What do you miss the most?"
  "Is there a story you'd like to tell? I've got time."
  "How are you holding up? The true answer is fine."
  "Is there anything I can do, even a little thing?"
  "Would it help to say their name out loud?"
@rule grief.more.ask_lost act: ask_about tags: nojoke
  "Do you ever think about {lost}? I do. I'd like to hear your stories."
@rule grief.more.continue act: continue tags: nojoke
  "Go on. I'm listening. There's no rush."
  "Take your time. I'm right here."
  "Tell me more, if you'd like. I'll just be quiet and hear it."
  "Keep going. You're doing fine."
  "I'm still here. Say it however it comes."

# ---- going along with it ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.backchannel act: backchannel tags: nojoke
  "[SAD]Mm. I hear you."
  "Yeah. Of course it does."
  "That makes sense. All of it."
  "I know. I know. Take a breath."
  "Mm-hm. Keep going, if you like."
  "That sounds like love, to me."
  "I'm right here. I'm not going anywhere."
  "Mm. That's real."
@rule grief.more.agree act: agree tags: nojoke
  "Yes. Exactly. It's a lot."
  "I think so too. It's the quiet that gets you."
  "You're right. There aren't any right words."
  "Yeah. It's heavy. We can set it down for a minute, though."
  "I agree. We should be gentle with each other."
  "True. It doesn't stop mattering. And that's okay."
@rule grief.more.disagree act: disagree tags: nojoke
  "I don't think it's small. It's allowed to be as big as it is."
  "I'm not sure that's true. It matters. They mattered."
  "I'd say it's okay to hurt. Hurting doesn't mean you're doing it wrong."
@rule grief.more.thank act: thank tags: nojoke
  "Thank you. I really needed that."
  "Thanks. That was kind. It landed."
  "[SAD]Thank you for staying. That's the whole thing."
  "Thank you. I'll remember it."
  "That means more than I can say. So, thank you."
  "You're good to me. Thank you."
@rule grief.more.yes act: yes guard: !act=ask_fact tags: nojoke
  "Yes. Please. That would help."
  "Yes. That sounds nice. Thank you."
  "I'd like that. Yes."
  "Yes. I'd really like that, actually."
@rule grief.more.no_hug act: no guard: act=hug tags: nojoke
  "Not just now. Thank you, though. I mean it."
  "I need a little space. I'm not shutting you out."
  "Maybe later. Please don't take it personally."
@rule grief.more.no_favor act: no guard: act=ask_favor tags: nojoke
  "I can't, not today. I'm sorry. Ask me again soon."
  "Not right now. I have no strength left today. Soon, though."

# ---- complaining, said softly: the speaker's own heavy day (asked how they are) ---------------------------------
@rule grief.more.complain act: complain guard: act=ask_feeling tags: nojoke
  "[SAD]It's been a heavy week. I'm trying to be gentle with myself."
  "Tired. The kind of tired sleep doesn't fix."
  "Sad. Quietly. Mostly I'm sad quietly."
  "Not great. But thank you for asking. Most people don't."
  "Some days it's like carrying a coat that's too heavy. Today's one."

# ---- a promise, after a goodbye ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.promise act: promise guard: act=farewell tags: nojoke
  "I'll check on you tomorrow. I promise."
  "I'll leave the light on. You know where I am."
  "Come back whenever. I'll be here. I promise."
  "I'll save you a seat. Anytime."

# ---- hello and goodbye -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.greet act: greet tags: nojoke
  "Hi. It's good to see you. I'm having a quiet day."
  "Hello. Come in. I'm glad you're here."
  "Hi, friend. It's a slow kind of day. Sit with me?"
  "Oh, hello. I'm a little sad today, but I'm glad it's you."
@rule grief.more.farewell act: farewell tags: nojoke
  "Goodbye. Look after yourself. Please."
  "Take care. Eat something. Rest."
  "Go gently. I'll be thinking of you."
  "See you soon. You're not alone, you know."
  "Bye for now. Come back anytime. I mean that."

# ---- not joking about it (a joke, a tease, a laugh at it); no cold shoulder, a plain no -------------------------------
@rule grief.more.dismiss act: dismiss guard: !pact=ask&!pact=open&!pact=flow&!act=compliment&!act=promise&!act=hug&!act=complain tags: nojoke
  "No. Not that one. It's too close."
  "Please don't. That one's not for laughing."
  "Ask me anything else. Not this one."
  "[SAD]That one's tender. Let's leave it alone."
  "I know you don't mean harm. But please. Not this."

# ---- romance about it: not now, kindly --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grief.more.deflect act: deflect_romance tags: nojoke
  "Not now. My heart's somewhere else today. Thank you for understanding."
  "Please. Not with this on me. I hope you understand."

# ---- comfort: another resident's reaction to a grief line (agree or backchannel) ----------------------------------------------
@rule comfort.more.agree act: agree tags: nojoke
  "Yes. And you don't have to be fine."
  "We're all thinking of you."
  "That's right. We've got you."
  "Yeah. We'll sit with you. As long as you like."
  "Yes. It's okay to take all the time."
  "We love you. Remember that."
@rule comfort.more.backchannel act: backchannel tags: nojoke
  "[SAD]I'm sorry too. We're here."
  "Whenever you're ready. We're not going anywhere."
  "Mm. We'll keep the lights on."
  "You're not alone. Not one bit."
  "Let us bring something. Please."
  "We'll look after each other."
@rule comfort.more.adult act: backchannel guard: !kid_present tags: nojoke
  "I'll put the kettle on. Nobody has to say anything."
  "Come by any time, day or night. I mean it."
